/ Without an address, the row keeps its place while the figures load. The
  value follows its label, and the chevron the value. All three stand in
  the middle, so they stay together over the width of both columns. A tap
  colors the row like a figure, because a row this wide would shrink too
  far with the click animation.
= content_tag (href ? :a : :div), href:, class: ['flex min-h-12 items-center justify-center gap-3 rounded-xl bg-fill px-4 py-3 text-fg-secondary', ('active:bg-fill-strong lg:hover:bg-fill-strong focus-ring' if href)] do
  span.truncate.text-sm.font-medium => t('car_breakdown.savings')
  span.flex.shrink-0.items-center.gap-2.font-semibold.tabular-nums.text-fg
    = value
    - if href
      = icon 'chevron-right', class: 'text-sm text-faint'
